# AI-ONLY NOTE: new, the directory FreeBSD 2.2.8, NetBSD 1.3 and OpenBSD
# keep GNU's programs in (gnu/usr.bin/gdb in each), with FreeBSD 2.2.8's
# gnu/Makefile as it stood but for its list: usr.bin alone, which holds
# gdb (docs/roadmap.md, item 3). Lite2 kept GNU's programs in contrib/,
# which is the sources, and in usr.bin, ld and gprof; the BSD
# makefiles that build GNU's sources are what this holds.
SUBDIR= usr.bin

